{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Which object slots a verb needs within arm’s reach, as opposed to merely in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"view. Declared by every row of both halves of the standard table — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CoreVerb"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StubVerb"},{"type":"text","text":" — so the answer is stated once per verb and derived from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"there."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Reach"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"mentions":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AddingCustomVerbs"],"kind":"mentions"},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Parser scope is the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"visible","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" set, which admits what can be seen through the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"glass of a shut jar or in somebody else’s hands. Much of the table is fine"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with that — you can smell a fire across a room, count coins behind glass,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"examine a thing you will never touch — and much of it is nonsense at a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"distance, so the answer is per verb rather than a blanket guard."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Three cases and not a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Bool"},{"type":"text","text":" because the two-slot shapes disagree with each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"give X to Y"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"put X in Y"},{"type":"text","text":" have to reach the recipient, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"throw X at Y"},{"type":"text","text":" must "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"not","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" have to reach the target, which is the whole point"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of throwing. Nothing wants the indirect object alone: the two-slot verbs that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"care about the container also want the thing going into it, and a direct"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"object already in the player’s hands passes for free."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Public because a game’s own verb has to be able to say it: a custom verb"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that carries its own default line — "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/action(_:reach:say:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"siblings — declares this column exactly as the two halves of the standard"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"table do, and it is the only place an invented verb can state what it has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to touch."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"enum","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"Gnusto"}],"externalID":"s:6Gnusto5ReachO","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Reach"}],"roleHeading":"Enumeration","title":"Reach","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Reach","kind":"identifier"}]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/gnusto\/reach"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Enumeration-Cases","title":"Enumeration Cases","identifiers":["doc:\/\